(2633942, 362489, 38032, '<td valign="top">this is funny to me simply because it looks like something I would do :)  ...  I like the idea a great deal.  I think it needs something  - like more of a view of the face.   I''m not really a big fan of the color just because it has eliminated white and that high tonal range.  I would suggest using a desaturation effect with on an RGB image and use "colorize" which will give you a more complete tonal range.  Hopefully this makes sense and hopefully you use photoshop because that''s what I''m talking about.  I did locate a movie link to illustrate a good way to do this:<br/>//www.photoshopsupport.com/tutorials/tt/adjustment-layer-mov.html</td>', 'this is funny to me simply because it looks like something I would do :)  ...  I like the idea a great deal.  I think it needs something  - like more of a view of the face.   I''m not really a big fan of the color just because it has eliminated white and that high tonal range.  I would suggest using a desaturation effect with on an RGB image and use "colorize" which will give you a more complete tonal range.  Hopefully this makes sense and hopefully you use photoshop because that''s what I''m talking about.  I did locate a movie link to illustrate a good way to do this://www.photoshopsupport.com/tutorials/tt/adjustment-layer-mov.html', '2006-07-18 19:38:25.000000', NULL, 1),
