(2639651, 361491, 50127, '<td valign="top">Rabits are hard to rehab.  They have incredibly weak immune systems because all the antibodies they get comes from their mothers milk- something we cant provide with kitten milk replacer or all those other formulas people recommend.  Therefore, as soon as they encounter any harmful bacteria (especially E.coli)... thats it, there is nothing you can do.  I had a bunny just about that age a little earlier this summer, it had taken a trip in a dogs mouth and he didnt make it through the night :(<br/> <br/>It was nice of you to try and save him.<br/></td>', 'Rabits are hard to rehab.  They have incredibly weak immune systems because all the antibodies they get comes from their mothers milk- something we cant provide with kitten milk replacer or all those other formulas people recommend.  Therefore, as soon as they encounter any harmful bacteria (especially E.coli)... thats it, there is nothing you can do.  I had a bunny just about that age a little earlier this summer, it had taken a trip in a dogs mouth and he didnt make it through the night :( It was nice of you to try and save him.', '2006-07-19 19:56:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2639660, 361491, 37961, '<td valign="top">Sweet little thing. Poor baby.</td>', 'Sweet little thing. Poor baby.', '2006-07-19 19:59:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(2639700, 362294, 11793, '<td valign="top">congrats - would have gotten hign marks from me in perspective II as well.  only negative is the clipping of the elbow - but minor.<br/> <br/>well done again !<br/></td>', 'congrats - would have gotten hign marks from me in perspective II as well.  only negative is the clipping of the elbow - but minor. well done again !', '2006-07-19 20:21:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2639728, 359868, 30982, '<td valign="top">The focus on the droplets is very good!  You could crop it down to the top of the white diamond to get rid of the greenish cast in the upper right corner, or you could fix that in editing.  Now that the challenge is over, take it back and edit it the way you want!</td>', 'The focus on the droplets is very good!  You could crop it down to the top of the white diamond to get rid of the greenish cast in the upper right corner, or you could fix that in editing.  Now that the challenge is over, take it back and edit it the way you want!', '2006-07-19 20:30:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2639769, 362176, 30982, '<td valign="top">I see from your photographer''s comments (and thanks for including those, by the way!) that you''d have preferred to have shot at a different time of day.  I hate including that in my comments (but I did anyway) because I fully understand that sometimes you shoot when you can!</td>', 'I see from your photographer''s comments (and thanks for including those, by the way!) that you''d have preferred to have shot at a different time of day.  I hate including that in my comments (but I did anyway) because I fully understand that sometimes you shoot when you can!', '2006-07-19 20:46:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2639820, 359557, 5885, '<td valign="top">I think I would have shot this without the sheet. Perhaps in a room that looks like it might have once been a child''s room or maybe an empty room. I think it would have had less of a sterile feel.</td>', 'I think I would have shot this without the sheet. Perhaps in a room that looks like it might have once been a child''s room or maybe an empty room. I think it would have had less of a sterile feel.', '2006-07-19 21:05:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(2639923, 362524, 30982, '<td valign="top">Congrats on an EXCELLENT finish (and thanks for your comments on my entry, too.)  Three challenges so far and all good results - keep it up!</td>', 'Congrats on an EXCELLENT finish (and thanks for your comments on my entry, too.)  Three challenges so far and all good results - keep it up!', '2006-07-19 21:34:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2639984, 362140, 30982, '<td valign="top">I really rather like this one - I was one of your 7''s.  In reading your comments, I''m kinda glad you didn''t have room to crop - I like the ramp coming down, and the glimpse of the cars.  I can''t see anywhere to crop!</td>', 'I really rather like this one - I was one of your 7''s.  In reading your comments, I''m kinda glad you didn''t have room to crop - I like the ramp coming down, and the glimpse of the cars.  I can''t see anywhere to crop!', '2006-07-19 21:44:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2640079, 361962, 20530, '<td valign="top">This is an interesting and well though out image. Love the blue BG. I don''t find the yellow/green cast in the smoke especially appealing. It could be unavoidable, or perhaps it was intended as part of the statement; but aesthetically, it doesn''t do much for me. <br/> <br/>I find it humorous that the first thing I thought was "Cingular". What a sad statement about our society that marketing has permeated our ability to view art objectively! On the other hand; it does say something about the quality of your composition. Definitely catchy.<br/> <br/>The FG is nice and the holes create repetition and mimic the shapes of the beakers. However, it seems as though the focus is on the FG at the expense of what I consider the most important elements (beakers).<br/> <br/>The organic shapes are very nice and I find myself looking for patterns in the smoke, as I do in clouds. Despite the minor technical foibles, I find this to be a very strong image.</td>', 'This is an interesting and well though out image. Love the blue BG. I don''t find the yellow/green cast in the smoke especially appealing. It could be unavoidable, or perhaps it was intended as part of the statement; but aesthetically, it doesn''t do much for me.  I find it humorous that the first thing I thought was "Cingular". What a sad statement about our society that marketing has permeated our ability to view art objectively! On the other hand; it does say something about the quality of your composition. Definitely catchy. The FG is nice and the holes create repetition and mimic the shapes of the beakers. However, it seems as though the focus is on the FG at the expense of what I consider the most important elements (beakers). The organic shapes are very nice and I find myself looking for patterns in the smoke, as I do in clouds. Despite the minor technical foibles, I find this to be a very strong image.', '2006-07-19 22:06:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2640244, 362367, 36382, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your red.  It''s a great picture.</td>', 'Congrats on your red.  It''s a great picture.', '2006-07-19 22:44:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2640254, 360209, 36382, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot.  Congrats on your yellow.  What impresses me most is the reflection of the smoke on the water.</td>', 'Beautiful shot.  Congrats on your yellow.  What impresses me most is the reflection of the smoke on the water.', '2006-07-19 22:46:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(2640292, 362351, 59415, '<td valign="top">Sorry I got 10th place.  I didn''t mean to steal your excellent photo''s place on the first page.  Great Job!</td>', 'Sorry I got 10th place.  I didn''t mean to steal your excellent photo''s place on the first page.  Great Job!', '2006-07-19 22:51:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(2640313, 362351, 30982, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by boomtap:</b></div><hr/><i> Sorry I got 10th place.  I didn''t mean to steal your excellent photo''s place on the first page.  Great Job! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>LOL!  Nah, I couldn''t have missed 10th to a nicer person or a better picture.</td>', 'Originally posted by boomtap: Sorry I got 10th place.  I didn''t mean to steal your excellent photo''s place on the first page.  Great Job!   LOL!  Nah, I couldn''t have missed 10th to a nicer person or a better picture.', '2006-07-19 22:55:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(2640317, 360335, 32754, '<td valign="top">this was one of the best photos...truly incredible shot.</td>', 'this was one of the best photos...truly incredible shot.', '2006-07-19 22:56:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2640636, 362524, 60275, '<td valign="top">This is GREAT! Thank you all for taking the time to vote. My 3rd challenge and managed to climb in 5th place. Further more, Im so happy for the 30+ comments  the greatest encouragement of all, especially after getting the shot only a few minutes before deadline. As with all my other entries, I barely had enough time to crop, resize and save. Therefore, this 5th place is a good incentive to find more time for photography (including post-processing). <br/> <br/>Now, back to earth ;) The way the setup was done, if anybody interested:<br/> <br/>- orange background<br/>- base : matte printer paper rest with a circular hole a bit smaller than the globe (enough to keep it ¾ above)<br/>- globe: 1$ glass globe (Dollarama)<br/>- lights: one underneath (flashlight), one lateral (reading flashlight) behind a Coca-Cola glass to throw those flames at the background<br/>- ice: chopped ice around the globe  not so easy to keep it there at about 28C<br/> <br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-07-20 10:04:27.</i></td>', 'This is GREAT! Thank you all for taking the time to vote. My 3rd challenge and managed to climb in 5th place. Further more, Im so happy for the 30+ comments  the greatest encouragement of all, especially after getting the shot only a few minutes before deadline. As with all my other entries, I barely had enough time to crop, resize and save. Therefore, this 5th place is a good incentive to find more time for photography (including post-processing).  Now, back to earth ;) The way the setup was done, if anybody interested: - orange background- base : matte printer paper rest with a circular hole a bit smaller than the globe (enough to keep it ¾ above)- globe: 1$ glass globe (Dollarama)- lights: one underneath (flashlight), one lateral (reading flashlight) behind a Coca-Cola glass to throw those flames at the background- ice: chopped ice around the globe  not so easy to keep it there at about 28C ', '2006-07-20 00:19:40.000000', '2006-07-20 11:04:27.000000', 0),
(2640656, 362367, 58840, '<td valign="top">wow, one of the coolest shots i have ever seen!</td>', 'wow, one of the coolest shots i have ever seen!', '2006-07-20 00:26:25.000000', NULL, 0),
